{
 "_about": "Colour and detail rules for the PMG's 3D model (tools/build_model.py). Rules are tried top to bottom against each CAD mesh name; the first match wins. A mesh whose rule names no colour takes its colours from the atlas: the MRA's for the parts the kits share (the I/O module, the Nano). The source is pmg-guide.glb, the CAD cut down by make_source.py (one copy of each part, where it sits built; the I/O module turned the published way up; the MRA's Nano as NANO; the four button caps renamed by colour). First draft 19 Oct 2026, from docs/research/pmg/reuse_plan.md.",
 "source": "pmg-guide.glb",
 "source_scale_to_mm": 1000,
 "palette": {
  "edge": "#111111",
  "wood": "#deb887",
  "steel": "#a6a9aa",
  "black_plastic": "#1e1616",
  "white_plastic": "#f5f5f6",
  "pcb_blue": "#224bbe",
  "pcb_navy": "#000f41",
  "pcb_black": "#1e1616",
  "pin": "#a6a9aa",
  "pin_silver": "#a6a9aa",
  "metal_can": "#a6a9aa",
  "ic_black": "#191919",
  "header_black": "#181818",
  "header_yellow": "#ffff80",
  "plug_grey": "#404040",
  "cap_tan": "#a5936d",
  "wire_brown": "#7c5a30",
  "wire_red": "#ef3340",
  "wire_orange": "#ff851b",
  "wire_yellow": "#ffdc00",
  "wire_green": "#3d9970",
  "wire_blue": "#0074d9",
  "wire_purple": "#a75294",
  "wire_grey": "#737980",
  "wire_white": "#f2f2f2",
  "grey": "#a6a9aa",
  "ink": "#1e1616",
  "lead_brown": "#975100",
  "lead_red": "#bd291f",
  "lead_orange": "#ff9d07",
  "sticker_white": "#ffffff",
  "sticker_black": "#1a1a1a",
  "sticker_blue": "#0074d9",
  "cable_black": "#2d2926",
  "sticker_off_black": "#181818",
  "jumper_cap": "#404040",
  "cap_black": "#1e1616",
  "cap_yellow": "#ffdc00",
  "cap_white": "#f5f5f6",
  "cap_blue": "#0074d9",
  "led_white": "#ffffff",
  "led_face": "#1e1616"
 },
 "defaults": {
  "color": "grey",
  "edge_angle": 40,
  "simplify_mm": 0.04,
  "edge_min_size_mm": 0.0
 },
 "rules": [
  {
   "match": "^USB Right Angle$",
   "color": "black_plastic",
   "components": [
    {
     "rank": [
      1,
      2
     ],
     "color": "pin"
    }
   ],
   "simplify_mm": 0.03,
   "max_tris": 3000,
   "outline": true,
   "_about": "the USB cable's right-angle Mini-B end (NAUO282), 3 solids: overmould black, the plug's shell and its insert silver (as the MRA's straight Mini-B: plug silver, the rest black). Not in the MRA or RCC: their Mini-B end is straight (docs/research/pmg/reuse_plan.md 2.3)."
  },
  {
   "match": "^USB Cable end$",
   "color": "black_plastic",
   "components": [
    {
     "rank": 1,
     "color": "pin"
    },
    {
     "rank": 2,
     "color": "white_plastic"
    },
    {
     "rank": [
      3,
      4
     ],
     "color": "pin"
    }
   ],
   "simplify_mm": 0.03,
   "max_tris": 4000,
   "outline": true,
   "_about": "the USB cable's A end (NAUO283): the same mesh as the MRA's usb-a-end.glb (vertices identical), the MRA's ^USBCableend$ rule renamed: overmould black, shell and contacts silver, tongue white"
  },
  {
   "match": "^H([1-9]|1[0-4])(v2)?$",
   "color": "wood",
   "simplify_mm": 0,
   "roughen_mm": 0.1,
   "engraving": "ink",
   "_about": "the laser-cut wood, H1 - H14 (four H9 keys; H4v2, H11v2, H12v2, H13v2): roughened as every kit's wood (publish.py requires it)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Wire Cap( V2)?$",
   "color": "jumper_cap",
   "_about": "jumper wire caps (the 34 the STEP has on the built parts' pins, and the 8 make_source.py copies onto V4 - V7 and the buttons' GND pins): #404040 as the MRA's (its atlas; the PMG Cadasio has them #000000, the rulebook's Dupont housings #1e1616)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Board\\^Big Button Module",
   "color": "pcb_navy",
   "simplify_mm": 0.02,
   "_about": "the button modules' boards (rulebook: PMG button boards #000f41)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Socket_Blok$",
   "color": "pin",
   "components": [
    {
     "rank": 1,
     "color": "header_black"
    }
   ],
   "_about": "a button module's header pin (rank 0, the bent pin, silver: Lee's pins-silver ruling; Cadasio #c6c1bc) and its black spacer (rank 1; Cadasio #1a1a1a). The CAD has four per module, two of them the same pin in the same place."
  },
  {
   "match": "^Tactal Switch",
   "color": "black_plastic",
   "simplify_mm": 0.05,
   "max_tris": 3000,
   "edge_min_size_mm": 1.5,
   "_about": "the 12 x 12 mm tactile switch (21 solids: the body and 20 small marks 0.25 mm thick on it), all black (Cadasio #1e1e1e)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Push_Button_Cap black$",
   "color": "cap_black",
   "simplify_mm": 0.05,
   "max_tris": 1500,
   "outline": true,
   "_about": "NAUO76 (D4); renamed by make_source.py (the four caps are one mesh in the CAD)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Push_Button_Cap yellow$",
   "color": "cap_yellow",
   "simplify_mm": 0.05,
   "max_tris": 1500,
   "outline": true,
   "_about": "NAUO83 (D5)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Push_Button_Cap white$",
   "color": "cap_white",
   "simplify_mm": 0.05,
   "max_tris": 1500,
   "outline": true,
   "_about": "NAUO84 (D6)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Push_Button_Cap blue$",
   "color": "cap_blue",
   "simplify_mm": 0.05,
   "max_tris": 1500,
   "outline": true,
   "_about": "NAUO85 (D7)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Push_Button_Cap",
   "color": "cap_black",
   "simplify_mm": 0.05,
   "max_tris": 1500,
   "outline": true,
   "_about": "a cap not renamed: should not happen with pmg-guide.glb"
  },
  {
   "match": "^Display TM1637",
   "color": "pin",
   "components": [
    {
     "rank": 0,
     "color": "pcb_blue"
    },
    {
     "rank": 1,
     "color": "led_face"
    },
    {
     "rank": 2,
     "color": "ic_black"
    },
    {
     "thin": [
      0,
      0.02
     ],
     "color": "led_white"
    }
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "box": [
      [
       -13.7,
       -6.45,
       1.35
      ],
      [
       15.7,
       6.45,
       8.25
      ]
     ],
     "color": "led_face"
    },
    {
     "box": [
      [
       -13.7,
       -6.45,
       8.45
      ],
      [
       15.7,
       6.45,
       8.55
      ]
     ],
     "color": "led_face"
    }
   ],
   "simplify_mm": 0.02,
   "_about": "the TM1637 4-digit display (NAUO79), one mesh of 41 solids, the same solids as TechBox's Cadasio model: rank 0 the board, which in this CAD includes the display block, blue #224bbe (rulebook); rank 1 a black shell 0.1 mm over the block (Cadasio #000000); the two boxes make the block itself black under it (its sides and top; not the segments' pockets' rims, 8.25 - 8.45); rank 2 the TM1637 chip under the board; the 30 flat segment and colon pieces (0 thick, own z 8.3, in pockets of the block) white; the 4 bent pins and their 4 stubs silver."
  },
  {
   "match": "^PCB$",
   "color": "pcb_blue",
   "simplify_mm": 0.03,
   "max_tris": 6000,
   "edge_min_size_mm": 1.0,
   "_about": "the LED matrix's board (Cadasio #234bbf ~ the house display blue)"
  },
  {
   "match": "^8x female rounded header$",
   "color": "header_black",
   "simplify_mm": 0.05,
   "max_tris": 1500,
   "edge_min_size_mm": 1.5,
   "_about": "the eight 8-way sockets between the matrix board and its four LED blocks (11,951 vertices each, all but hidden): kept light"
  },
